+
+A CPU capture at 2× density may prepare a text cache when a value edit arrives
+during a full capture that takes at least 250 ms. The slow fixture holds the real
+full-image decode for 300 ms and records the measured capture interval. The next
+edit must use the prepared painter without another upstream capture. The complete
+original image must publish before preparation starts, and preparation must not
+publish a paint. Quiet focus, a pending edit during a capture below 250 ms, other
+densities, and GPU storage must keep the ordinary capture path.
+
+A transparent input exposes the root background, checking that the retained SVG
+includes paint removed from the background cache's foreground image. This static
+fixture disables the input's transition and restores its original inline style.
+An unsupported SVG or a seed containing only spaces must fall back to upstream region capture.
+Refresh, density replacement and disposal before preparation starts must cancel
+it without parsing, allocating a painter or publishing a late frame. A later
+ordinary capture must still be able to prepare a painter after a rejected seed.
